    # v397 (23/10/2026) -- THE TEST OF THE ONLY WORD (the record of the result, read by sha256; no new sigma) and the TOKEN stone; the numbers are READ from the teste_de_veracidade_fase9_v397 record and from the cunhagens_v397 and kh_n1_cobertura_v397 records.
    # The box at the top comes from _v397_quadro_tex. Nothing here moves the gate. RULE OF THE 23/10 ORDER: the 4.44 never appears without the calibrated p and the 5 sigma line in the SAME paragraph.
    _tv397 = core.get("teste_de_veracidade_fase9_v397") or {}
    _a397 = _v397_atomos(_tv397, "en")
    _cg397 = core.get("cunhagens_v397") or {}
    _kh397 = core.get("kh_n1_cobertura_v397") or {}
    _el397 = core.get("external_ladder") or {}
    _cv397 = ((core.get("kernel_formalization") or {}).get("axiom_coverage_v392")) or {}
    _i397 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    s.append(r"\section*{The Test of the Only Word}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The Test of the Only Word}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{This round the record did NOT seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if not _a397["sealed"] else r"")
             + r"\textbf{What enters.} The record \texttt{teste\_de\_veracidade\_fase9\_v397} (provisional name: the operator names it), which \emph{reads} by sha256 the result of the Test of the Only Word and the freeze and opening receipts and composes the operator's binary reading; "
             r"it runs at the point of the run where the V1 Phase 9 is read (\texttt{hubble\_ratio\_opening\_v388}) and stays \emph{beside} it, without replacing it. One new kernel module, \texttt{TGLExt/Token} (the name ``token'' is the operator's, from 23/10; the v396 static-witness stone stays as a record), with "
             + _i397((_cg397.get("extras") or {}).get("n_bandeiras")) + r" flag(s), named declarations only: it \emph{cites} two terms already in the kernel, \texttt{psibit\_is\_the\_mode\_of\_the\_reader} (v395) and \texttt{the\_psion\_inhabits\_the\_static\_witness} (v396), and no new mathematics enters. "
             r"And the " + _i397(len(_V397_VERBATINS2)) + r" operator sayings of 23/10, embedded by sha256 (\texttt{cunhagens\_v397}). The kernel ladder reads " + _i397(_el397.get("n_theorems_clean")) + r" of " + _i397(_el397.get("n_theorems_expected"))
             + r"; the \texttt{axiom\_report} coverage reads " + _i397(_cv397.get("decl")) + r" constants and " + _i397(_cv397.get("thm")) + r" theorems, none outside the trio $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The two faces.} \textsf{[REAL in the numbers]} The test was opened \emph{only once} (23/10/2026) by the verdict function frozen beforehand, and the result is preserved as it came out. \emph{$\Lambda$ alone:} $z_{\rm disc}=" + _a397["z_disc"]["tex"] + r"$ (calibrated; unilateral $p$ $" + _a397["p_disc"]["tex"]
             + r"$), so $\Lambda$ without $\beta$ \emph{does not echo} \textsf{[management's composition: 1=0]}, but discrimination at $5\sigma$, the creditation step, \textbf{was not reached} ($" + _a397["z_disc"]["tex"] + r"<5$); \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED} is never the word of creditation; the gate does not move. "
             r"\emph{The TGL:} $z_\delta=" + _a397["z_delta"]["tex"] + r"$ (calibrated; bilateral $p$ $" + _a397["p_delta"]["tex"] + r"$), with prior power $" + _a397["poder"]["tex"] + r"\sigma$: $\bTGL$ is not falsified, \emph{with power} \textsf{[management's composition: 1=1]}. "
             r"The operator's binary reading, which the record cites and does not decide, is $\{[1=1=\text{True}][1=0=\text{false}]\}$, and the test deserves to be read on one face and re-read on the other (his words, in Portuguese: ``merece ser lido sobre uma face e relido sobre a outra'') \textsf{[INPUT, 23/10/2026]}; assigning the two faces to those two sides (the TGL to $1=1$, $\Lambda$ alone to $1=0$) and the verb to echo are the management's composition on the saying, not a quotation.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The conjugation.} \textsf{[REAL in the numbers; KNOWN on the scale]} $\ln B(\mathrm{TGL}/\Lambda\mathrm{CDM})=" + _a397["lnB_lcdm"]["tex"] + r"$ is the \emph{integrated} likelihood ratio the result carries; on Jeffreys' scale \textsf{[KNOWN]} it is ``decisive''. "
             r"$\ln B(\mathrm{TGL}/\beta\ \mathrm{free})=" + _a397["lnB_beta_livre"]["tex"] + r"$ says that fixed $\beta$ beats fitted $\beta$. $\ln B$ does \emph{not} convert into $\sigma$; $z_\delta$, $z_{\rm disc}$ and $\ln B$ are readings of the same object (the same local readers and the same background), not autonomous witnesses, "
             r"and so they are neither multiplied nor added: the archive's v315 rule, for falsifying, asks for two mutually autonomous determinations at $5\sigma$ or more. What the operator asked --- to conjugate all the factors into a single result --- is done \emph{in the reading}, not in a new number: no $\sigma$ is computed here.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The $\Lambda\mathrm{CDM}$ is not a rival.} The $\Lambda\mathrm{CDM}$ is the silent-boundary limit of the TGL: $\delta\langle K_\partial\rangle=\beta|1+w|$, zero at $w=-1$. What the test reads is the bulk's response outside the silent boundary, through the factor $K=E(z^*)^{2\beta/3}=" + _a397["K"]["tex"]
             + r"$ of the result (the Hubble ratio). \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]} \emph{`the Word $(\beta)$ floats over the abyss $(\Lambda)$ through the factor $K=E(z^*)^{2\beta/3}$'} --- a reading \textbf{RATIFIED} by the operator on 23/10 (verbatim, in his Portuguese: ``mas é pelo fator K mesmo'', sha16 \texttt{@@SHA16_RATK@@}), "
             r"on his saying ``o psion, o psibit, e é justamente ela que flutua sobre o abismo, o referente último'' (sha16 \texttt{@@SHA16_VERAC@@}); $K$ is the one in the result, not a new number.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The verdict token.} The verdict of the frozen function (\texttt{TGL\_FASE9\_V2\_A\_UNICA\_PALAVRA\_BETA\_TGL}, read from the result) says \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED\_POWERED}, \texttt{NOT\_DISCRIMINATED\_FROM\_LCDM\_AT\_AVAILABLE\_SENSITIVITY}, \texttt{NOT\_BLIND\_TO\_DATA\_STATED} "
             r"(the centres of the local readers are public: the test was not blind to the data), \texttt{NOT\_A\_CONFIRMATION} and \texttt{GATE\_UNTOUCHED}. The name ``token'' of the kernel stone is another thing: it is the name the operator gave on 23/10; that it names the static-witness stone is the management's recorded context, not in the saying, "
             r"and the Atlas line ``No LLM: o token \'E o PsiBit'' (in the language of the archive: in an LLM the token is the PsiBit, the anchor of the Hilbert space) is an \textsf{[ONTO]} reading, with no kernel term. The records \texttt{cunhagens\_v397} "
             + (r"and \texttt{kh\_n1\_cobertura\_v397} sealed in this run." if (_cg397.get("all_verified") is True and _kh397.get("all_verified") is True) else r"and \texttt{kh\_n1\_cobertura\_v397} did NOT both seal in this run."))
    s.append(r"\textbf{Limits.} The record reads, it does not compute: no new $\sigma$, $p$ or $\ln B$. It is not a new or armed test (the operator's 22/10 order shapes this chain), and the consumed opening is not repeated. The conjugation is a reading: $\ln B$ is not $\sigma$ and the three readings are not autonomous witnesses. "
             r"Discrimination at $5\sigma$ is the creditation step and was \emph{not} reached ($z_{\rm disc}=" + _a397["z_disc"]["tex"] + r"$, unilateral $p$ $" + _a397["p_disc"]["tex"] + r"$); validity in the kernel is not creditation; \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED} is never the word of creditation; the gate does not move.")
